      "text": "```\nCNT COMPOSITE MECHANICS\n========================="
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#010",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
        "canonical_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[applications]",
        "current_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Why CNT in polymer:\n  MWCNT Young's modulus: 200-500 GPa\n  Epoxy matrix Young's modulus: 3-5 GPa\n  Rule of mixtures (upper bound for aligned):\n    E_composite = f * E_CNT + (1-f) * E_matrix\n    At f = 0.05 (5 vol%): E ~ 0.05*350 + 0.95*4 ~ 21.3 GPa\n    Compare to neat epoxy: 4 GPa -> 5x improvement"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#011",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
        "canonical_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[applications]",
        "current_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BUT: real composites don't reach rule of mixtures\n  Reasons:\n    1. CNT misalignment (random orientation reduces benefit by ~5x)\n    2. Poor CNT-matrix interface (slippage instead of load transfer)\n    3. CNT agglomeration (bundles don't disperse as individual tubes)\n    4. Length limitation (aspect ratio controls load transfer efficiency)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#012",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
        "canonical_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[applications]",
        "current_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Practical improvement (MWCNT/epoxy, 1-2 wt%):\n    Tensile strength: +10-30%\n    Fracture toughness: +20-50% (CNT bridging cracks is the mechanism)\n    Electrical conductivity: +10^6 (percolation threshold at ~0.1 wt%)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#013",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
        "canonical_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[applications]",
        "current_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "BOEING 787 LIGHTNING STRIKE PROTECTION:\n  Fuselage: carbon fiber reinforced polymer (CFRP) -- excellent structural properties\n  PROBLEM: CFRP is electrically less conductive than aluminum\n    Lightning strike: current must disperse; CFRP alone causes delamination\n  SOLUTION: CNT-enhanced outer ply (copper mesh is alternative, heavier)\n    MWCNT percolation network provides conductivity\n    Current disperses over larger area -> less localized damage\n    Weight saving vs. copper mesh: ~20-30 kg per aircraft"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#014",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
