        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Clay structure:\n  Montmorillonite (MMT): 2:1 phyllosilicate\n  Platelet structure: 1 nm thick, 100-500 nm lateral\n  Layer spacing: 1.2 nm (natural), expandable by intercalation\n  Aspect ratio: 100-1000 (high -- good for barrier properties)\n  Surface: negatively charged (cation exchange capacity)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#018",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
        "canonical_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[applications]",
        "current_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Nanocomposite fabrication:\n  1. MELT BLENDING: clay + polymer + extruder\n     Simplest; often doesn't fully exfoliate clay\n  2. SOLUTION INTERCALATION: swell clay in solvent, mix polymer\n     Better exfoliation possible\n  3. IN-SITU POLYMERIZATION: monomer + clay, then polymerize\n     Best exfoliation (Toyota Nylon-6/MMT 1988 -- historic first)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#019",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:nanotechnology:09-applications, git-history:nanotechnology:09-applications]",
        "canonical_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "concepts": "[applications]",
        "current_path": "nanotechnology/09-APPLICATIONS.md",
        "id": "maxim:nanotechnology:applications",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "nanotechnology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[applications]",
        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Morphologies:\n  a. INTERCALATED: polymer chains between layers, layer spacing increased\n     (better than conventional but not optimal)\n  b. EXFOLIATED: layers fully separated, dispersed in polymer matrix\n     (optimal -- maximum aspect ratio, maximum interface area)"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#020",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
