        "section": "nanotechnology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Nanotechnology Applications: Nanocomposites, Coatings, Catalysis, Energy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Mechanism:\n  Silica nanoparticles (5-100 nm, amorphous SiO2): two effects:\n  1. POZZOLANIC REACTION:\n     SiO2 (nano) + Ca(OH)2 (portlandite from cement hydration)\n     -> C-S-H (calcium silicate hydrate, the binding phase)\n     Converts weak Ca(OH)2 crystals -> additional strong C-S-H\n  2. FILLER EFFECT:\n     NP fill inter-particle voids between cement grains\n     Denser packing -> lower porosity -> lower permeability"
    },
    {
      "id": "09-APPLICATIONS.md#025",
      "path": [
        "09-APPLICATIONS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
